import Bitcoin.SigHash.Interface
import Bitcoin.Serialization.Interface

/-!
# BitcoinProofs.Property.Y09 — property-test corpus for Sighash/BIP143

Systematic edges + seeded-random segwit-v0 spends, checked against a PYTHON
ground-truth reference written from
bip-0143.mediawiki (@ bips 927b6de) and Bitcoin Core @ cce32b168
(interpreter.cpp:1609-1687 legacy / :1633-1670 WITNESS_V0) — NOT from the
Lean code. The reference was validated BEFORE any Lean contact against two
independent corpora: 4/4 BIP143 worked examples and 500/500 legacy rows of
`spec/vectors/core/sighash.json`.

REPRODUCIBLE: the generator regenerates this file byte-for-byte; every pseudo-random case derives from
`random.Random(20261016)`. Digests are asserted in INTERNAL sha256d byte
order (the order the BIP text itself prints; sighash.json prints the
GetHex()-reversed order).

Proof tiers (why not every case is a digest `rfl` — see F-Y09-001):
  * BULK: preimage-level assertion `bip143MsgL/legacyMsgL .. = <python
    preimage>` by kernel `decide`, with BIP143's three dshaL sub-hashes
    rewritten by the shared staged theorems `dsha0..` below.
  * DIGEST (key cases): adds the full digest via two single-SHA256 stages
    (`mid_*`/`dig_*`) joined by rewrite; a one-shot rfl through double-
    SHA256 exceeds kernel recursion depth (probes 18-25).
  * Totalization probes (oor nIn, legacy SINGLE-overflow): cheap `decide`.
All 122→104 case expected values come from the python reference; a Lean
mismatch would surface as a failed `decide`/`rfl` here.

Sections:
  A  BIP143 official worked examples (7, all digest-tier)
  B  hashtype matrix + raw-bit hashtypes + amount-commitment contrast (19)
  C  SIGHASH_SINGLE range grid + tri-modal legacy contrast (14)
  D  amount edges incl. int64 two's-complement wrap (10)
  E  scriptCode edges: CS-prefix boundaries, 0xab splicing contrast (14)
  F  structural edges: versions, sequences, empty vout, NULL prevouts (8)
  G  seeded pseudo-random segwit-v0 spends (24 + 6 legacy) + totalization
     probes; includes fully-random uint32 hashtypes (htBase totality)
-/

namespace BitcoinProofs.Property.Y09

open Bitcoin.Data Bitcoin.SigHash Bitcoin.Serialization

set_option maxRecDepth 4000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

/-- `(Array.range 8).map f` unfolds to the explicit 8-element array.
Kernel-reducible bridge for `Sha256.compressLoop`'s state-add (core's
`Array.map = Id.run <| as.mapM` is monadic and kernel-opaque). -/
theorem mapRange8 {α : Type} (f : Nat → α) :
    (Array.range 8).map f = #[f 0, f 1, f 2, f 3, f 4, f 5, f 6, f 7] := by
  have hr0 : (Array.range 0) = #[] := rfl
  simp only [hr0, Array.range_succ, Array.map_append, Array.map_empty]
  simp

